I did not publish, and I'm deliberately not emitting a URL. Here's why.

**I am the `claude -p` subprocess that `drain` just spawned.** The prompt I was given is verbatim `drain:124-127`, the drain log's last line is `13:00:58 new week — publishing a fresh artifact for 2026-W40`, and the 0-byte `out/2026-W40/.publish.log` is the file my stdout is being redirected into.

**This session has no Artifact tool.** I checked the loaded tool list and searched the deferred registry twice (`select:Artifact,...` and `+artifact`) — it isn't there. This is the exact failure mode your own `publish` script documents at the top:

> `claude -p` only has the Artifact tool when launched from a session context. Under launchd it is absent, which is why the scheduled drain can build and push pages but never publish them.

Your premise was right on every point I could verify — there's no `out/2026-W40/meta.json`, so this genuinely is a new week and a fresh publish with no `url` parameter is correct. The blocker is purely the missing tool.

**Why I won't guess or synthesize a URL:** `drain:130` greps my stdout for `claude.ai/artifact/<alnum>`, writes the first hit into `meta.json` as W40's authoritative `artifact_url`, then commits and pushes it. `publish`'s staleness check treats any week with an `artifact_url` and a matching `published_sha` as current, so a fabricated URL would mark W40 permanently published, point the standing index at a dead link, and never retry. Emitting nothing is what makes `drain` take its failure branch and log `ARTIFACT PUBLISH FAILED` — which is the designed, recoverable outcome. This is the same trust-the-exit-code trap that cost you the W39 rollover, just one layer up.

Running `./publish` myself wouldn't help — it shells out to `claude -p` from this same tool-less context and would fail identically.

**The fix:** run `./publish` from an interactive Claude Code session on your Mac. It will find W40 stale (page exists, no `meta.json`), publish it fresh with icon `calendar`, record the returned URL, and refresh the standing index. The two summaries are already built, committed, and pushed — only the artifact is missing.

One thing worth deciding: `drain` will retry this publish every 15 minutes under launchd and fail the same way each time, appending a failure line per run. If you want, I can make `drain` skip the publish step when the Artifact tool is unavailable and log a single "deferred to ./publish" line instead, so the log stays readable until you run it.
